cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool, please cite it as below."
title: "Supply Chain Ordering Policy Tester: which ordering rule should one stage of a supply chain use?"
abstract: "An interactive simulator of a four-stage supply chain (the Beer Game chain) that compares order-up-to, smoothed order-up-to and pass-through ordering rules on stage cost and the bullwhip effect, with built-in checks for the order-up-to target, information sharing, the backlog-vs-lost-sales cost model and the smoothing trade-off, plus a playable 36-week ordering game against rule-based and human-heuristic bots. All data are simulated."
authors:
